My wizard started with a wand of polymorph, which I began desperately
began using after Thoth, merely satisfied, did not care to feed his
fainting supplicant. I was in an armor shop on level 3, so this was not
something I could have fixed with theft, nor where there any nearby kobold
corpses I could have turned into something more edible.

Hoping to turn myself into something without a stomach, I began zapping
myself. First go: grid bug, very unhelpful in the long run; I had to drop
everything but the wand. Frankly, I felt very lucky to be able to use it
again; I didn't know grid bugs had hands. *Zap* a starving gnome again.
*Zap* and now I'm a starving silver dragon. Well, this seemed better,
except for the fainting part. "If Thoth won't feed me," I thought, "then
I'll just have to chow down on the shopkeeper." Not enough power for the
breath weapon, but a nice few rounds of claw/claw/bite should do the trick
when I've got 107 HP to play with. 

Then I fainted from lack of food and woke up a gnome once again, standing
next to an angry, still living shopkeeper. DYWYPI? And, uh, Thoth was
angry at me; well, the feeling was mutual, birdbrain. 

